From 350c80238307425bf30bd8b5cd871e176f3075cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:45:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: complete regd_update_completed when a country
 change is rejected

ath12k_reg_chan_list_event() leaves pdev_idx at 255 on the
ATH12K_REG_STATUS_DROP path (e.g. firmware rejects the requested
country), so the 'out' label never finds an ar and never signals
regd_update_completed. ath12k_regd_update() then waits for the full
ATH12K_REG_UPDATE_TIMEOUT and logs 'Timeout while waiting for
regulatory update'. Resolve the pdev from the event's phy_id on the
DROP path when it is in range so the waiter is released.

dodge trial (local only).
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
index 3c5eb8d88..cc6da2cb3 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
@@ -6992,6 +6992,8 @@ static int ath12k_reg_chan_list_event(struct ath12k_base *ab, struct sk_buff *sk
 		 * not going to create new regd for it
 		 */
 		ret = ATH12K_REG_STATUS_VALID;
+		if (reg_info->phy_id < ab->num_radios)
+			pdev_idx = reg_info->phy_id;
 		goto mem_free;
 	}
 
